{"clock":1,"nonce":"02ae6d63772d32540ba4670608c4d36e","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793807402,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6206257177"},"data":{"body":"Follow-up of #76 (PR #81).\n\n**Now.** The sync lock and its journal are in the machine's folder (`.git/board/sync.lock`, `core/syncer/lock.go`). On a git board that's right: each clone has its own copy and merges. On a shared datastore (PostgreSQL), two machines can run a forge sync on the same board at once. Each sees an issue unlinked and creates it on the forge: two forge issues for one git-board issue. Same for comments posted twice.\n\n**Want.** A run takes a lock the datastore holds when it is shared:\n- a `datastore.Locker` capability (`Lock(ctx, name) (unlock func(), err error)`), checked by type assertion as the others;\n- PostgreSQL: `pg_try_advisory_lock` on a key from the board's database, held on one connection for the run; `syncer.Running` asks it too;\n- git, Markdown files, forge only: the machine's file lock, as today.\n- The journal (a cut run's progress) stays per machine: a run going on from another machine's cut run is out of scope.\n\n**Acceptance.**\n1. Two `syncer.Sync` on one PostgreSQL board from two `pgstore.Store`s: the second answers `ErrLocked` while the first runs (test against `GIT_BOARD_TEST_POSTGRES`).\n2. A process killed mid-run leaves no lock (the session's end frees it).\n3. git boards unchanged.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","title":"datastores: one forge sync at a time per board, not per machine"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793822098,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6206257177"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793822098,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:6206257177"},"data":{"add":["bug"],"remove":null}}]}